<title>GERMANY: Messer Griesheim sees better '97 earnings.</title>
<headline>Messer Griesheim sees better '97 earnings.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany industrial gases producer Messer Griesheim said on Wednesday it planned to post a sharper rise in turnover in 1997 than 1996's 3.2 percent.</p>
<p>The company's managing director, Herbert Rudolf, told a news conference that net profit would grow at a similar rate to sales while pre-tax profit will rise at a faster pace.</p>
<p>He gave no precise forecasts.</p>
<p>Rudolf said the company, a unit of Hoechst AG, planned to invest 580 million marks in fixed assets this year.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
